From: Toon Verwaest <verwaest@chromium.org>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 14:04:55 +0200
Subject: [parser] Parse dynamic import arguments as AssignmentExpression

ParserBase::ParseImportExpressions previously parsed both the module
specifier and import options using
ParseAssignmentExpressionCoverGrammar() instead of
ParseAssignmentExpression(). Because dynamic import arguments cannot be
binding patterns or arrow formal parameters, using the cover grammar
left pending expression errors (such as `{x = z}`) unvalidated in the
enclosing ExpressionParsingScope, allowing a subsequent destructuring
assignment (e.g. `import({x = z}, [a] = [])` or
`1 + {x = z} + import([a] = [])`) to clear the expression error.

Use ParseAssignmentExpression() for both arguments of import().

Bug: 567222737
